fernande@galaxy.cps.msu.edu (Jose R Fernandez) writes:
>What's the difference between being stunned and being confused?

	Stunned is when you're wandering around dazed, with no control over
your direction except that you can stand still if you want.  Also, if you
bump into your pet, it has the same effect as if you simply tried to move to
where your pet is.  "Your stupid mutt is in the way."
	If you're confused, you have more control over your movement, but if
you bump into your pet it's as if you attacked it.  Also, being confused can
have certain advantages:

You can rustproof your weapon or armor by reading a scroll of enchant weapon/
armor while in a confused state.  This won't work if you're stunned.
	Here's a little tip in case you're stunned or confused and want to do
something on the square you're on, like picking a chest lock:  when it asks 
for a direction, use ">" instead of "." .  Normally you could use either one,
but if you're stunned, the game interprets "." to be a movement direction.  
But as far as I know, ">" is always interpreted as meaning down.
